  entry .Version
    info
        - the identification string this client sends: `SSH-2.0-susurration_0.72`
        + la chaîne d'identification qu'envoie ce client : `SSH-2.0-susurration_0.72`
    detail
        - The line sent, terminated by CR LF, before anything else (RFC 4253 §4.2), and the text
        - hashed into the exchange hash as `V_C`. The server's own line is `Transport#serverVersion`.
        + La ligne envoyée, terminée par CR LF, avant toute autre chose (RFC 4253 §4.2), et le texte
        + haché dans le hachage d'échange en tant que `V_C`. La ligne propre du serveur est
        + `Transport#serverVersion`.
  entry .Message
    info
        - the message numbers of RFC 4250 §4.1.2, as named `Byte` constants
        + les numéros de messages de la RFC 4250 §4.1.2, sous forme de constantes `Byte` nommées
    detail
        - The first byte of every packet's payload names its message. These are the numbers the
        - transport, authentication and connection protocols use: `Disconnect` (1), `Ignore`
        - (2), `Unimplemented` (3), `Debug` (4), `ServiceRequest` (5), `ServiceAccept` (6),
        - `ExtInfo` (7), `KexInit` (20), `NewKeys` (21), `KexEcdhInit` (30), `KexEcdhReply`
        - (31), `UserauthRequest` (50), `UserauthFailure` (51), `UserauthSuccess` (52),
        - `UserauthBanner` (53), `UserauthPkOk` (60), `GlobalRequest` (80), `RequestSuccess`
        - (81), `RequestFailure` (82), `ChannelOpen` (90), `ChannelOpenConfirmation` (91),
        - `ChannelOpenFailure` (92), `ChannelWindowAdjust` (93), `ChannelData` (94),
        - `ChannelExtendedData` (95), `ChannelEof` (96), `ChannelClose` (97), `ChannelRequest`
        - (98), `ChannelSuccess` (99) and `ChannelFailure` (100).
        + Le premier octet de la charge utile de chaque paquet nomme son message. Voici les numéros
        + qu'utilisent les protocoles de transport, d'authentification et de connexion :
        + `Disconnect` (1), `Ignore` (2), `Unimplemented` (3), `Debug` (4), `ServiceRequest` (5),
        + `ServiceAccept` (6), `ExtInfo` (7), `KexInit` (20), `NewKeys` (21), `KexEcdhInit` (30),
        + `KexEcdhReply` (31), `UserauthRequest` (50), `UserauthFailure` (51), `UserauthSuccess`
        + (52), `UserauthBanner` (53), `UserauthPkOk` (60), `GlobalRequest` (80), `RequestSuccess`
        + (81), `RequestFailure` (82), `ChannelOpen` (90), `ChannelOpenConfirmation` (91),
        + `ChannelOpenFailure` (92), `ChannelWindowAdjust` (93), `ChannelData` (94),
        + `ChannelExtendedData` (95), `ChannelEof` (96), `ChannelClose` (97), `ChannelRequest`
        + (98), `ChannelSuccess` (99) et `ChannelFailure` (100).

        - They are what `Transport#expect` takes and what a `Wire.Writer` begins a payload
        - with:
        + C'est ce que prend `Transport#expect` et ce par quoi un `Wire.Writer` commence une charge
        + utile :

        ```scala
        import soundness.*

        val writer = Wire.Writer()
        writer.byte(Ssh.Message.ServiceRequest)
        writer.text(t"ssh-userauth")
        writer.data
        ```
